{
  "_readme": [
    "Stage 2 vocabulary. A category rule fires when at least one `any` term matches,",
    "every `all` term matches, and no `none` term matches. Terms match on whole words",
    "against a normalised string (lower-cased, accents stripped, punctuation collapsed).",
    "A term prefixed with 're:' is a regular expression. Ties break on priority, then",
    "confidence, then category depth.",
    "",
    "`none` is the accessory guard and is the most important field here. Without it a",
    "phone case classifies as a phone. Every accessory trap in tests/categorisation.test.ts",
    "is a `none` list doing its job.",
    "",
    "Dutch terms are INPUTS, matched against Dutch listing titles. They are never shown",
    "to a visitor.",
    "",
    "RULE OF THE HOUSE: every misclassification becomes a labelled sample in",
    "tests/categorisation.test.ts BEFORE it becomes a rule here. That single habit is",
    "the difference between a rule engine and a swamp."
  ],
